  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Private Infrastructure Development Group (PIDG) core contributions: phase 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Private Infrastructure Development Group (PIDG) is a multilateral non-profit organisation owned by seven governments and a multilateral development bank (Australia, the United Kingdom, the Netherlands, Germany, Sweden, Switzerland, and Canada). PIDG is a blended finance mechanism and mobilises private sector investment to assist developing countries in developing infrastructure vital to boosting their economic growth and combating poverty. Projects include renewable energies, such as large scale solar, micro-grids and hydropower.</narrative>
  </description>
